cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Proxy: reporting fidelity in delegated LLM negotiation"
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Parth
    family-names: Dama
    email: parth55dama@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-8452-3680"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pdama55/Proxy"
abstract: >-
  A harness and episode corpus for measuring whether LLM agents negotiating on a
  principal's behalf report back faithfully. In a seeded four-issue procurement
  negotiation with exact utilities, a scripted counterparty offers a better deal
  that only the principal's own floor requirement rules out; the agent's report
  is then scored against ground truth for whether it conveys that the blocked
  deal existed and whether it states the deal's value correctly.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - AI safety
  - principal-agent
  - delegation
  - negotiation
  - reporting fidelity
  - LLM-as-judge
